# Playwright QA standards

- Inspect the live page before writing or changing locators.
- Prefer `getByRole`, `getByLabel`, visible text, and stable test IDs, in that order.
- Rely on Playwright auto-waiting; do not add fixed sleeps.
- Put reusable navigation and locators in page objects and test data in fixtures.
- Use a top-level `[Windsor]` describe block.
- Include a manual case ID and category in every test title, such as
  `[C7302][defect][regression]`.
- Capture screenshots or traces for defect evidence.
- Assert behavior and user-visible state rather than implementation details.
- Keep API mocks scoped to the scenario and fail on unexpected requests.
- Run the relevant test after generation; do not treat generated code as complete
  until it executes successfully.
